From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:01:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: connect native pools and scanout buffers

Carry the fixed-pool map response and guest dma-buf contract from
Droid-VM 20f1e3a2, 93e158d2 and 1ef32747d through the pinned rutabaga
bridge to the unified renderer. Preserve the existing byte-offset ABI
without another runtime SHARE for pool-resident resources.

Connect the scanout layouts from 8883a20c2 and 8b754f606 to the common
CPU converter and Wayland blitter. Retain guest iovecs and a scanout
handle, including RGhA, while keeping Linux's existing texture import
path. The Wayland blitter completes its guest-buffer read before the
virtio response. Blob test fixtures now supply their wire layouts.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 release build and all guest argument matrices
TEST=14 GPU tests, 12 display/input tests, native pool allocator test

Purpose: Connect native pools and scanout buffers.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
